From af8acb42778b276976b21bda76204953a1ed664f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Lucas Garfield (depsolve-perf prototype)" <proto@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:22:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] solver: add opt-in package_metadata level to the V2 API

The V2 depsolver API always returns the full RPM package metadata that
the solver model knows about (NEVRA, checksums, header checksum,
license, summary, description, vendor, packager, url, source RPM,
build time, sizes, group, reason, all reldeps and the file list).

To be able to measure what that costs, and to give callers that only
need manifest data a cheaper path, add an optional request field
`arguments.package_metadata`:

  - "full" (default): unchanged behaviour.
  - "minimal": only name, epoch, version, release, arch, repo_id,
    location, remote_locations and checksum are returned for depsolve,
    dump and search. Both the DNF4 and DNF5 solvers then skip reading
    the other attributes from DNF entirely, so the cost of extracting
    the metadata is saved too, not just the cost of serializing it.

The V1 API is not affected; it has its own fixed representation.
